digits_order, digit_endianness"] [555 29 "// -1: least significant first"] [556 29 "// -1: little-endian digits"] [560 2 "// PyType_Freeze (Objects/typeobject.c): Py_TPFLAGS_IMMUTABLETYPE set, every other type of the MRO immutable already"] [577 2 "// ---- Python/import.c: PyImport_ExecCodeModule and its variants (module_dict_for_exec, _fix_up_module, the code"] [578 2 "// run in the module's dict) ----"] [598 5 "// PyModule_NewObject takes any name (its __name__): a module made bare, the name in its dict"] [691 2 "// ---- Objects/frameobject.c ----"] [734 2 "// ---- Objects/fileobject.c: PyFile_FromFd, _io.open(fd, mode, buffering, encoding, errors, newline, closefd) ----"] [753 2 "// ---- Objects/unicodeobject.c, Objects/bytesobject.c: the charmap codec, the FS converter, escapes ----"] [773 84 "// PyErr_BadArgument"] [803 22 "// Py_CLEANUP_SUPPORTED"] [824 2 "// ---- Python/pyhash.c: PyHash_GetFuncDef, a static PyHash_FuncDef {hash, name, hash_bits, seed_bits} ----"] [837 2 "// ---- Objects/codeobject.c: PyCode_NewEmpty(filename, funcname, firstlineno) ----"] [847 3 "// the compiled code object is a step, not the result: the code watchers see one CREATE, the replaced object's,"] [848 3 "// as PyCode_NewEmpty makes one code object (queue 274b, 274's Low)"] [860 3 "// co_firstlineno is left (pyi's code.replace refuses it: its code is its IR; a Low of queue 270b)"] [863 2 "// ---- Modules/gcmodule.c: PyGC_Enable, Disable (the previous state), IsEnabled, over the gc module ----"] [888 2 "// ---- Python/pythonrun.c: PyRun_String, PyRun_SimpleString, Py_CompileString and their Flags variants, over"] [889 2 "// compile(), exec() and eval() ----"] [903 26 "// PyCF_IGNORE_COOKIE: the bytes are UTF-8 whatever their coding cookie says"] [910 3 "// the C API's compiler takes cf_flags as they come; compile() refuses a bit outside PyCF_MASK, PyCF_MASK_OBSOLETE"] [911 3 "// and PyCF_COMPILE_MASK, so the others go (py-eval-1122: test_run's run_anyfileflags passes closeit's 1 as cf_flags)"] [919 73 "// run_eval_code_obj's"] [946 3 "// PyErr_Print: sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback)"] [982 2 "// ---- PyRun_File, PyRun_SimpleFile, PyRun_AnyFile and their Ex and Flags variants (py-eval-1122): the FILE's text"] [983 2 "// read whole by the world's fread (closeit: fclose'd once read, as pyrun_file's parser closes it), then run as the"] [984 2 "// string functions run theirs; _PyRun_SimpleFileObject's __main__: __file__ and __cached__ set for the run when it has"] [985 2 "// no __file__ (removed after), __loader__ a SourceFileLoader for a file not \"<stdin>\"; an error printed, -1 ----"] [1090 52 "// flush_io"] [1100 3 "// PyErr_Print: sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback)"] [1119 2 "// PyRun_InteractiveOne, InteractiveOneFlags, InteractiveOneObject and InteractiveLoop, InteractiveLoopFlags: the"] [1120 2 "// FILE's text parsed (ast.parse; a SyntaxError of the filename), each statement compiled alone in 'single' mode (an"] [1121 2 "// expression's value shown by sys.displayhook) and run in __main__; One runs the first and gives -1 for an error, Loop"] [1122 2 "// runs them all, an error printed and the next statement run, and gives 0 (the prompts, stderr's in CPython, not"] [1123 2 "// written); an error printed by sys.excepthook (PyErr_Print)"] [1227 2 "// PyRun_AnyFile*: a FILE that is no terminal runs as PyRun_SimpleFile* (_Py_FdIsInteractive: pyi's interactive"] [1228 2 "// flag is never set in a C caller's run, so only a tty would be the interactive loop, which is not given)"] [1239 2 "// ---- Objects/abstract.c: the number protocol's rest ----"] [1260 4 "// ternary_iop: the in-place slot first, called without the modulo (slot_nb_inplace_power: in-place power"] [1261 4 "// does not pass the third argument to __ipow__), then ternary_op's pow"] [1272 2 "// ---- Python/pystate.c, ceval.c: one thread state, the GIL's release a no-op (pyi's world runs on one thread) ----"] [1276 4 "// sizeof(_PyThreadStateImpl) (936 on LP64, queue 568: the inline _Py_MakeRecCheck of a Py_BUILD_CORE_MODULE"] [1277 4 "// module reads its c_stack_soft_limit, at 848; zero, so no C stack check fires)"] [1285 2 "// legacy subinterpreters (py-eval-1122; Python/pylifecycle.c's Py_NewInterpreter and Py_EndInterpreter, pystate.c's"] [1286 2 "// PyThreadState_Swap, as _testcapi's run_in_subinterp calls them): Py_NewInterpreter makes and enters pyi's legacy"] [1287 2 "// subinterpreter (ExtNewInterpreter: the calling thread now runs in it, so the C API's calls that follow, the run of"] [1288 2 "// a string among them, are the subinterpreter's) and gives a thread state of its own; Py_EndInterpreter leaves and"] [1289 2 "// ends it; PyThreadState_Swap records the current state (the switching is ExtNewInterpreter's and ExtEndInterpreter's)"] [1297 2 "// PyGILState_GetThisThreadState: the thread's current state (one thread state a thread here)"] [1330 31 "// Py_EndInterpreter leaves no current thread state"] [1333 2 "// ---- Objects/abstract.c: the number protocol's operators, over the operator module ----"] [1373 2 "// ---- Objects/bytearrayobject.c ----"] [1380 42 "// ob_start (the mirror's storage, queue 270)"] [1385 1 "// littleEndianFlag is _resolve_endianness: -1 or Py_ASNATIVEBYTES_NATIVE_ENDIAN's bit is the platform's (little), else"] [1386 1 "// the low bit."] [1389 1 "// fitsInBits is _fits_in_n_bits: v in [-2^(b-1), 2^(b-1))."] [1398 1 "// asNativeBytes is PyLong_AsNativeBytes (Objects/longobject.c, 3.14.10): v written into the n bytes at buf as two's"] [1399 1 "// complement (truncated), the bytes it needs returned; CPython's compact ints (one 30-bit digit) as an ssize_t."] [1422 2 "// the n low bytes of v's two's complement, little-endian"] [1427 19 "// big-endian"] [1444 26 "// _PyLong_IsCompact"] [1473 4 "// -(2^(8n-1)): every bit used, no extra sign bit"] [1492 1 "// The C API's legacy subinterpreters (Py_NewInterpreter): those not ended yet by thread state, in the order made, and the"] [1493 1 "// current thread state when it is a subinterpreter's or NULL (subCurSet; subCur 0 and subCurSet false: the main one's)."] [1501 1 "// endLeakedSubs ends the subinterpreters an entry's C made and did not end (py-eval-1122: _testcapi's test_atexit"] [1502 1 "// reaches a native pyi does not provide after Py_NewInterpreter, and the unwinding skipped its Py_EndInterpreter, so the"] [1503 1 "// thread stayed in the subinterpreter: later tests saw its sys.stdout, warnings and ast); run when the outermost entry"] [1504 1 "// leaves, newest first, the thread back in the main interpreter."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[42 25] [288 24] [349 25] [453 30] [461 14] [461 21] [498 13] [498 33] [531 27] [531 34] [537 22] [537 30] [572 23] [593 27] [594 48] [603 48] [610 52] [614 41] [622 50] [627 51] [632 53] [643 62] [646 45] [669 33] [674 34] [678 80] [799 27] [870 38] [939 77] [947 21] [948 51] [1003 27] [1068 24] [1072 70] [1091 37] [1092 47] [1101 21] [1102 51] [1125 21] [1126 51] [1136 24] [1262 43] [1326 18] [1341 32] [1354 32] [1428 13] [1428 40] [1475 21] [1475 38] [1506 28] [1506 36] [1507 32]]} (go/file "capi_port.go" :imports [

